<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santissima Trinità di Saccargia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1116</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Saccargia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Santissima Trinità di Saccargia is a Romanesque church near Codrongianos in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>, consecrated in 1116 and given by the judges of Logudoro to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camaldolese">Camaldolese</a> monks. Built in Pisan style of alternating black basalt and white limestone, it has a tall bell tower and a later portico, and its apse preserves 12th-century frescoes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santissima-trinita-di-saccargia.jpg" alt="Santissima Trinità di Saccargia" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julius Barclay · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Basilica_of_Saccargia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
